{
  "doc": "Shared parity fixture for the persisted Project wire shape (ship review Phase 2a, defect 3 — pattern copied from layout_parity.json). The Rust test (src-tauri/tests/project_parity.rs) deserializes `project` into models::Project, re-serializes, and asserts EXACT JSON equality — a field dropped, renamed, or defaulted by the Rust shape fails per-key. The TS test (src/lib/__tests__/projectPersistence.test.ts) loads the SAME fixture and runs it through the actual canonical auto-save path (hydrateProjectState -> buildSavePayload), asserting deep equality — a field dropped by the save path fails there. AUTHORING RULES: (1) every Project field must be present, populated, and NON-default so a drop-to-default is detectable; (2) optional serde fields (skip_serializing_if) must be present-with-value or absent, never null; (3) every Rust f64 field must be float-formatted (14.5, 90.0 — never 14 or 90) or serde_json Value equality fails on integer-vs-float repr; (4) map_settings must populate every key of the TS DEFAULT_MAP_SETTINGS or the load-path merge adds keys and the TS round-trip fails; (5) schema_version must equal CURRENT_SCHEMA_VERSION (asserted — re-author this fixture on every schema bump); (6) working_color_space has a single variant today which serde always skips on serialize — the Rust test documents this one exception. When you add a persisted field to models::Project / types.ts Project, add it here (and to PROJECT_WIRE_KEYS in the TS test) or the suites fail.",
